  "worked_solution": "First, we must find the elements of the sets $A$ and $B.$\n\n- The elements of the set $A$ are all the natural numbers that satisfy the inequality $-1\\le x+1\\le 3,$ that is to say, $-2\\le x\\le 2.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nA={1,2}.\n$$\n\n- On the other hand, the elements of the set $B$ are all integers that satisfy the inequality ${x}^{2}\\le -2.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nB=\u2205.\n$$\n\nNow, let's inspect the given statements.\n\n- $A\u2286B$ is false, while $A\u2288B$ is true. For example, $0\\in A$ but $0\\notin B.$\n\n- $B\u2286A$ is true. The empty set is a subset of every set.\n\n- $A\u2287B$ is equivalent to $B\u2286A,$ which is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II, III, and IV only.\"",
